The optional src/login/provider and src/login/client_data implementations, their
tests and the tools/go-oracle/clientdata helper extract provider verification
and title metadata validation from cinnabar-mc/cinnabar. They retain the PolyForm
Noncommercial License 1.0.0 reproduced in LICENSE-CINNABAR. They are not covered by the root
crate's MIT/Apache license choice; individual source files identify this exception.

The bedrock-client, bedrock-client-tokio and bedrock-packs crates extract resource-pack negotiation,
caller-driven Tokio resolved/direct setup, settings/Login/pack wire effects and connection/transport
lifecycles, bounded transfer-target normalization, archive handoff and text
handling from cinnabar-mc/cinnabar. These extracted
implementations retain the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0 reproduced in
LICENSE-CINNABAR; they are not covered by the root crate's MIT/Apache license
choice. Their Cargo manifests identify that retained license explicitly.
The built-in resource-pack identity catalog follows the public Gophertunnel
behavior reference pinned in tools/go-oracle/go.mod. Its MIT notice is retained in
LICENSE-MIT-gophertunnel.

The batch codec is an original Rust implementation informed by public code in:

- bedrock-crustaceans/bedrock-rs (Apache-2.0), commit
  ab7bb9521af078d4094c86da8b127d5f53cf0d31.
- HashimTheArab/gophertunnel (MIT), commit 81e65c54fb21, including its
  declared-compression, batch-drop and outgoing packet-limit fixes.
- CloudburstMC/Protocol (Apache-2.0) and PrismarineJS/bedrock-protocol (MIT).

No source files from those projects are included. Their licenses continue to
apply to their respective projects. Dependencies carry their own licenses.

The optional RakNet driver uses bedrock-crustaceans/raknet (Apache-2.0), with a
Cinnabar ordering-window and offline negotiation fixes pinned in Cargo.toml.
The Go loopback fixture uses HashimTheArab/go-raknet (MIT), pinned in
tools/raknet-peer/go.mod. Neither dependency's source is vendored here.

The standalone probe consumes protocolgen's generated packet crate and uses
bedrock-crustaceans/nethernet (Apache-2.0), with Cinnabar client identity support
pinned in its manifest. It also uses bedrock-rs bedrock_auth for the caller-owned
ClientData metadata schema, under the Apache-2.0 commit identified above.
These dependencies are not vendored here.

The optional Login helpers use the same public Rust and Go references for
line-terminated token JSON, token-only offline requests, server key exchange and
authenticated player identity projection, including the XUID-derived UUID.
P-384 signatures, public-key parsing and ECDH use RustCrypto p384. The synthetic
Login oracle shares tools/go-oracle's existing Gophertunnel pin.

The original accepting pack/startup owner follows that same MIT Go reference
for delivery normalization, sequential chunk flushes and startup ordering. Its
conformance helper calls the actual pinned Go policy; no reference source is vendored.

The ClientData validator and Go field-fold/URL behavior follow the pinned
Gophertunnel Login owner (MIT) and Go encoding/json, net/url, unicode and x/text
(BSD-3-Clause). The actual Go generator checks the reflected schema and finite
Unicode/locale/JSON data on every oracle test run. These upstream notices are
retained in LICENSE-MIT-gophertunnel and LICENSE-BSD-Go.

URL-reference parsing follows the Go net/url package under its BSD license; see LICENSE-BSD-Go.

Auxiliary certificate decoding follows Go crypto/x509 and the cryptobyte
ASN.1 integer, framing and time rules under LICENSE-BSD-Go.
The protected x5c chain shape follows go-jose (Copyright 2014 Square Inc.) under Apache-2.0.
